    <briefdescription>
<para>Bench-level functional validation of the TLE92466ED driver against a 300 \u03a9 resistive load on a single channel. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Hardware:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>TLE92466ED evaluation board</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>VBAT \u2248 12 V</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>300 \u03a9 power resistor wired between channel output and GND</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Theoretical current at 100 % duty: I = VBAT / R = 12 V / 300 \u03a9 = 40 mA</para>
<para>This example sweeps the ICC setpoint from 5 mA to 40 mA in 5 mA steps, holds each step for 200 ms, and then reads the coherent feedback snapshot via ReadChannelFeedback() (atomic FB_FRZ/FB_UPD path added in Phase 6). It prints the programmed vs measured current and VBAT for each step so the operator can quickly confirm \u00b12.5 mA accuracy without needing an external multimeter.</para>
<para>Exit criterion: measured current for every step is within \u00b12.5 mA of the setpoint or limited by VBAT/R (whichever is smaller). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
